WEBVTT

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.900
Our peaceful lives have finally returned to us.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.950
Now that the culture festival is over, I finally realize...

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.530
I finally see what a blessing it is to have
ordinary days where nothing happens.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.070
It's so true.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.820
Good morning!

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.490
Good work on the school festival!

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.450
There's something different about you, Ishino.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.450
You think so?

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.570
If we don't hurry, we'll be late!

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.070
I've seen Ishino like that before when she was in love...

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.900
I guess she had a good experience at the culture festival.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.900
Ayado.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.780
Good... Good morning, Ayado.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.320
G-good morning to you, too!

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.360
Why were they acting like that?

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.240
I don't know if it's safe to ask.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.650
Ishino, huh?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.700
Yeah.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.950
Episode 15
Regarding My Unforseen Family Crisis.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.240
But I can't help thinking all that energy
is going to fade in about three days.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.610
Just a hunch.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.700
I hope it's a good guy this time. Her new crush.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.490
Yeah.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.490
And the festival committee reps from my class, too.
I think they're really hitting it off.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.400
Wow. It looks like the festival
was a success for everyone.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.570
That's good to know.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.700
You know, it's been a while.
I'd like to visit your house again.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.070
Okay.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.150
Yay!

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.110
I've missed talking to your mom.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.200
My life...

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.110
is so peaceful.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.610
So peaceful, it scares me.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.030
I'm getting a bad feeling about this.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.360
I should be careful.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.860
I'm home.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:08.950
What are you doing?

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:09.950
Yoga.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.240
I have a reunion coming up, so it's time to diet.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.900
I don't think losing a few pounds
will change anyone's opinion much.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.240
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.490
Believe it or not, when your mother was in school,

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:24.570
she was 45 pounds lighter,
and ridiculously popular with the guys.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.780
You shouldn't tell such obvious lies.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.070
Uh, yes, ma'am.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.280
Wh-what? Who is this?!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.240
I told you, it's me!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.400
Y-you're kidding!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.200
There's no way THIS is my mom!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.280
How rude.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:47.240
It's not like I was born your mother, you know.
Even I was young once.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.990
It's no use. My brain can't process it.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.570
Before

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.030
After
Before

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.610
And this is?

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.360
Oh, that's your father.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.030
So young...

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:58.400
He was already doing his research then.
He was modest and didn't really stand out.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.860
But he was your mother's most ardent admirer!

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.280
R-really...?

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.990
Oh, Nakagoshi! Lunch next week?

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.400
Uh-huh. We can leave the men. They'll be fine!

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.650
I never
wanted to know
that much about my
parents' courtship

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.610
Two o'clock, then! See you!

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.900
Big Brother! Are you there?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.320
I have a favor to ask.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.200
Can I borrow some money?

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.200
Here I thought you needed me,
but all you want is my money?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.110
Go ask Mom.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.200
I can't. I want to take Anzu to the aquarium.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.450
If I told Mom that, she'd give me too much grief.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.360
Does it have to be the aquarium?

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:37.570
Mm-hmm.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.570
Anzu really likes fish. I want to show her some.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.610
Fine. Here.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.450
I'll give you back whatever's left.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.030
And pay back the rest in installments.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.030
You're so conscientious.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.570
I just don't want to owe you too much.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.450
So how are things going with you and Anzu, anyway?

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.740
You know it's rude to ask that question.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.200
Oh...

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.200
It would be rude to ask him about what happened.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.150
I'm painfully aware of the fact
that there's nothing I can do to help.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.450
All I can do is stand back and watch.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.320
A three-day weekend!

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.780
What should we do?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.610
If there's something you want to do, I'm up for anything.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.400
Let's go on a trip!

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.450
A trip?!

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.740
WILD FANTASY INN

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.700
It was really nice in the hot spring.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.990
And look at this yukata!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.240
No, fantasy! Stop!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.280
Huh? Tsutsun?!

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.700
Sorry, can't do a trip.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.320
I'm scared enough of my current peaceful life.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.110
If I went on a trip like that, I think I very well might die.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.150
I was joking. And I'm sorry.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.700
O-oh... It was a joke.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:10.950
Chief, I think it would be better
if we stopped seeing each other.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.700
You have a wife and children.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.950
And here I... I'm sorry.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.820
No, it was my fault, too.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:23.400
Wh-what is this indecent couple doing
at a family restaurant in the middle of the day?

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.400
Anyway, let's go.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.070
Um... what's wrong, Tsutsun?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.280
Dad...

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.280
That was my dad.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.490
What?! No, but they were talking about...

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.950
I can't believe it.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:54.740
I thought he was a boring guy
who only ever thought about researching glue.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.740
FATHER, MITSURU
BEEN MAKING GLUE
FOR THE PAST 22 YEARS

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.570
I can't believe he was having an affair!

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.820
I mean, I know Mom has really let herself go,
but that's no reason!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.070
No, this has to be a misunderstanding!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.110
Were you listening...?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.990
That was clearly the talk of people
who were engaging in adulterous behavior.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.570
And he's a father with not one, but two children.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.740
That's despicable!

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.360
C-come on, he's your family!

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.530
What good will it do to not trust him?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.110
Yeah. You're right. Sorry.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.700
I'm sure it's okay!

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.700
I'm home...

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.990
Welcome back. Want some dinner?

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.700
Uh, no, I'm fine.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.650
Oh, really? You should have told me.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:34.900
S-sorry.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.650
Uh, hey! Hikari!

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.570
Dammit! I really wish I didn't have this secret!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.150
No! For now, I'm just going to trust him.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:44.110
Dad is not having an affair!

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.780
Besides, would a woman that young even like my dad?

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.240
Of course she wouldn't!

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.650
I need sleep.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.900
This is all just a bad dream.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:00.700
What's with the doom and gloom?

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.110
Oh, Hikari. Good morning.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.820
Hikari, take a seat.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.740
Wh-what's going on?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.280
You see, your father has been having an affair.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:13.570
Where are you going?

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:14.530
What do you mean?

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.150
Don't give me that nonsense!

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.030
I-I'm sure it's just a misunderstanding.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.110
Do you have proof?

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.030
I found this email, and this receipt for a fancy dinner.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.240
Italian Cuisine
From: Saori Kono
Thank you for yesterday
Dinner was delicious. Thank you so much.
2 Dinner Platters
I had a lot of fun!!

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.360
She's swimming in proof...

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.780
He betrayed me.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.400
No, wait, Mom! Don't cry! And you're old enough
to know better than to spy on people's email!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.740
First, you need to sit down and talk it out!

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.110
It's not what you think.
I bet it was just a friend from work!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.280
"Just a friend from work"
wouldn't send an email with that many emojis!

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.490
Come on, Dad, stand up for yourself!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.400
I'm sorry.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.570
I trusted you for 20 years...

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.900
Wh-whoa...

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:05.110
Somehow my family life has turned
into a soap opera. What's happening?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.780
Losing touch
with reality

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.110
Oh, wow.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:16.400
I knew something was wrong when you
randomly canceled our plans at your house.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.530
But wait, are you sure it's okay for you
to be hanging out with me like this?

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:21.950
It's fine.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.820
It's not like me staying at home would fix the problem.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.900
All I could do was make desserts.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.950
It really was the calm before the storm.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.610
When something good happens,
something bad is sure to follow.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.570
That's just how my life always goes.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.490
Right now, my time with you is the only peace I have.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.700
If anything happens, tell me right away.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.400
I will come to you whenever you need me.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:59.650
Thinking about it, Mom and Dad must have had
a time in their lives when they were just like us.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.070
And in that case,
I feel like everything is going to be okay.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:06.240
Yeah. We've had our fair share of fights, too.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.110
After 20 years as husband and wife,
they would have a bond that we just can't understand.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.400
It's going to be okay.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.780
You're right. Yeah.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.030
Divorce Papers

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.610
Wh-what are those doing here?!

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.530
What about your husband-and-wife bond?!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.200
Think this through, Mom!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.900
I have thought it through.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.110
We did have a bond. I trusted him.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:30.490
So I can't forgive him.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.450
All these years, I worked as a housewife for him
until I even looked the part.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.900
But if he's cheating on me, I can't do it.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.030
That... That's Dad's fault?

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:42.950
This is what happens to a woman when she's neglected.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.950
But even when he was so busy,
he came home late every night.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.990
Even when he slept through his rare days off, I didn't
mind,

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.900
because I thought he was working hard for his family.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:57.280
But how am I supposed to greet him
when he comes home from work every day?

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.950
D-Dad!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:00.860
I'm sorry.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.990
Don't you have more to say than "I'm sorry"?!
You can't just let it end like this!

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:07.650
I have never fought against
any of your mother's decisions.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:10.400
I know she's stubborn. It's no use trying to stop her.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:13.280
He... He's so passive about all this!

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.280
He's my dad, alright.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:19.200
There you have it. I will be taking my son
and going home to mother.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.950
Tell me you're joking! You can't do that!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:26.700
Hikari, you or Kaoru will be coming with your mother.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.450
Wha-!

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.780
This is too sudden!

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.110
Kaoru and I need time to process!

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:34.110
I mean... Mom's family...

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.530
...lives in Oshamambe!

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.990
Oshamambe

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.490
I'm sorry, Tsutsui.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.490
For dragging you out here.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.570
It's okay. I needed to get out of the house.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.990
When I'm alone, I keep dwelling on it...

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:53.150
and then I wish I could just disappear forever.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.150
Uh, I...

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.360
Is this... about Ayado?

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:00.490
Mm-hmm.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.950
I don't care if it's an illusion,
or a misunderstanding, or what...

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:12.530
I'm the worst.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.320
I don't think she even sees me as a friend anymore.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:19.570
When she saw me in the hall,
she wouldn't even look me in the eye.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.110
I'm so stupid.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.150
How could I have been so thoughtless?

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:25.900
I-I don't really know what happened.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.700
But I've done things like that!

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.150
I have tons of regrets!

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.860
And I'm not being comforting or helpful in any way!

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:33.740
No, you are.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:37.860
I'm sorry, it must sound like I'm talking to myself.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.700
I need to figure this one out on my own.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.530
It's just, talking to you helps me feel better, so...

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.700
Ito...

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.530
Actually, me too.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.030
O-Oshamambe?

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.740
What the heck?!

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:58.450
Who cares about my problems?!

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:00.860
You're in WAY more trouble than I am!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.820
No, it's pretty bad for both of us.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:06.110
I-if you went away, Tsutsui, I...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.780
No, sorry. It's okay.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:13.150
I mean, the logical thing is for her to take Kaoru,
since he's still in grade school.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.780
There's no way I'm going.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.700
And anyway, my parents are just
really worked up right now, that's all.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.030
R-really?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:22.650
Sorry. You're already upset about something,
and now I made it worse.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.900
We both have it rough.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.030
But we'll just do what we can, right?

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.700
Oh, Hikari. Welcome home.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.900
Th-thanks.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.700
To explain: His father has been camping out in the living room since the argument

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.650
Mom must have banished him from their room.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.110
You don't seem too upset, Dad.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.820
Is that what you think?

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.610
What are you going to do about this?

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:50.990
If your mother wants a divorce,
then I accept her decision.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.860
I never had the right to argue.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.990
It's true I was seeing another woman,
so I don't have any excuse.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:02.240
Neverpart Z

00:13:59.030 --> 00:13:59.990
Look, Hikari!

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:02.240
That glue... That's the one I made!
Neverpart Z!

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.610
We had a truck try to pull it off this time,
Even this truck will never pull them apart!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.070
but someday I want to see if we can use a jet.
Ooh, how strong!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.740
Neverpart Z

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.070
Neverpart Z, new formula on Zale now!

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.650
I probably shouldn't say this about my own father,
but what is wrong with him?

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.900
So what, you don't even care anymore?
About your own family?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.700
Of course I care.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:22.990
My heart is breaking right now.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:27.030
Your mother stayed with a loser like me for 20 years.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:30.280
She raised two strong kids.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:34.360
And I just figured, maybe I can't ask
for any more than that.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:37.360
Wow. He thinks just like I do.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:44.530
Your mom is such an upbeat, wonderful woman,
I'm sure she'll find a new life up in Hokkaido.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.610
No, no, no. She's nothing like she was
back in high school!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.400
I still love her.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.200
She hasn't changed at all.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:59.200
Anyway, it's been a long time since we've talked like this.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.820
I hear you have a girlfriend?

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:04.030
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.700
Of course, I heard about it ages ago.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:07.950
I'm happy for you.

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.110
I can't do it.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:15.030
I'm not used to talking to you about this stuff. Goodnight.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:17.650
It's ironic, isn't it?

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.320
I've spent my life trying to find a glue
that will hold anything together.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:24.740
But there is no glue that can keep
people's hearts from drifting apart.

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.030
I can't count on Dad to fix this.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.320
Benefits of Oshamambe, Hokkaido
Lots of fresh air
No traffic
A quiet town
Cheap rent

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.320
But if it were me, and she said...

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.650
I'm breaking up with you.

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:39.030
If she said that to me,
I'm pretty sure I would be paralyzed, too.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:41.200
Big Brother!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.650
What do you want, stupid? Try knocking!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:47.110
M-Mom and Dad say they're getting a divorce.

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:49.950
They said Mom's going to Hokkaido.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.900
So they finally told Kaoru.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:55.320
What's going to happen to me?

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.200
Oshamambe's a real nice place.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.490
You can play in the snow.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.240
I don't care about snow!

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.610
I'm staying in Tokyo, and no one's gonna stop me!

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.150
You go live in Oshamambe!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.240
What?!

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:10.650
You don't care where you live as long as
you have your games and anime, right?

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.240
Wha-! Don't make up my mind for me!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.240
Do you have any idea how hard it is
to transfer to a new high school?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.570
The logical thing would be to send the grade-schooler!

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.610
I'm just a kid!

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.900
Changes in environment are hard on me
physically and mentally!

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:27.820
And yet I have the least decision-making power
in our whole family.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:28.650
It's just not fair!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.820
This kid will be fine no matter where he goes!

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:37.110
Well what about me?! I'm definitely not cut out
for starting all over in a town full of strangers!

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:38.110
I can't do it, okay?!

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:40.150
That's just because you don't try!

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:43.740
It's what you get for actively avoiding human interaction!

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:46.860
If you're not gonna put in the effort,
then you don't get to claim the same rights as me!

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.650
What's gotten into you? You're scaring me!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:52.530
You're just in grade school!
Don't go attacking me with logic!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:55.570
Then give me a different reason that you can't go.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.070
I can't go...

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.070
Because she's here.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.200
Well... I have Anzu, too.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:16.990
Oh yeah.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:19.780
Good point.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:32.150
I'm going to be out of the house.
You'll have to order dinner for a while.
-Mom

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:31.700
How long is "a while"?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.200
She... ran away?

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.200
Uh, I'm just going out for a minute!

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.320
Takeout! Kaoru, what do you want for dinner?!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.860
I don't know what's going on, but tempura.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:46.740
Where would Mom even go?!

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:48.990
I have no idea!

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.900
Maybe I should go home and ask Dad!

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.200
I... I found her!

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:00.650
H-hi, Mom.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.150
Hikari.

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.610
Uh...

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.150
What do you want to order for dinner?

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.200
Kaoru wants tempura.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:15.240
Why don't we go home
before everyone worries about you?

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.700
Mom, seriously. Don't get a divorce.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.400
Don't worry. Oshamambe is a lovely place.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:29.650
Yeah, but I don't really want to change schools.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:33.950
You have always had a hard time making friends.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:35.700
Then I should take Kaoru.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:38.530
He's young, and still needs his mother.

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:40.110
Well...

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:43.280
Hikari
Kaoru
Oshamambe Meter

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:43.110
Sorry, Kaoru!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.570
Yeah. I think Kaoru does need his mom.

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:49.200
It's easier to adapt at a younger age, after all.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:53.070
He's a bright kid, and in six months,
he'll be having a grand time building snowmen.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.110
TSUTSUI DOING
HIS BEST TO GET
RID OF HIS BROTHER

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.610
That's true.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:19:01.780
But you, too, Hikari. You were so wrapped up in your
anime and video games, you never had many friends.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.070
But you've always been a kind boy.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.700
I love you both, very much.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:12.450
You are a handful, always doing
the most unexpected things.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:16.610
But compared to a boy who can handle anything
like Kaoru, you make things a little more interesting.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:18.450
No, I...

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:25.530
Hikari
Kaoru
Oshamambe Meter

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:22.450
Even now, your first instinct was to come find me.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:24.490
You gotta love those firstborn sons.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.700
Maybe you're the one...

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:27.450
Wh-whoa, wait a second!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:30.450
I am opposed to breaking up my family!

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:31.990
Absolutely against it!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:33.950
It's too late.

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:35.240
But why?!

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.860
Your father told me he was glad.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.740
A-about what?

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:46.360
He said he was happy when
that other woman told him she liked him.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.530
D-Dad...

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.400
Yeah, I was shocked, too.

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:55.450
I don't think he sees me as woman to love anymore.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.820
No, I don't think that's true.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:01.700
I-I'm sure that he's really sad... Not that I know.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:06.400
Even if he is, I just don't know
where we went wrong or how to fix it.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.530
Well, I suppose I could start by losing 45 pounds.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.280
Yeah, right.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.570
There's too much good food in Oshamambe.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.360
Crab and rice, crab cakes...

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:16.780
I'm begging you!

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:18.610
Come back to your senses!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:21.820
I talked to Dad! He said he still loves you!

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.320
And Kaoru and I both need you!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.610
Please!

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:33.610
I understand.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.280
Your mother has made up her mind.

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:41.070
So your mom's going to reconsider?

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.900
Well...

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.450
You always looked like there was nothing
going on in your head.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:52.570
But now I see you actually care
very deeply about your family.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:55.070
The oldest really is the best.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:04.570
I think I really would like you to be the one
that comes to Hokkaido with me.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.320
You will come with me, won't you, Hikari?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.990
Hikari
Kaoru
Oshamambe Meter
